---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import { BUSINESS, hasLicenceNumber } from '../data/business';
import { title, description } from '../lib/seo';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title('About Blouin Pest Services')}
  description={description(`${BUSINESS.owner.name} owns and runs Blouin Pest Services in Maine. Who does the work, what we hold, and how to check it.`)}
  path="/about/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'About', item: '/about/' }]}
>
  <h1>About Blouin Pest Services</h1>
  <p class="lede">{BUSINESS.owner.name} founded Blouin Pest Services in {BUSINESS.founded}. He does the inspections, the treatments and the follow-ups himself.</p>

  <p>
    I have seven years of pest control experience. I got my start working with my good friend Anthony Ciriello, who mentored me
    and taught me how to handle a wide range of pests and exclusion work. That hands-on experience shaped the way I run Blouin
    Pest Services today.
  </p>
  <p>
    When someone calls me about a pest problem, I want them to understand what I found, what I recommend, and what it will cost.
    I take pride in being honest and transparent with customers and in offering affordable service without leaving them guessing
    about the next step. I work to respond as quickly as possible, inspect carefully, and find the source of a problem instead of
    treating only what is visible.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every property and pest problem is different, so I build a plan around the situation in front of me. Whether I am helping a
    homeowner with carpenter ants, sealing rodent entry points, or working through an issue across several rental units, my goal
    is the same: provide the best service I can and be straightforward throughout the job.
  </p>
  <p><strong>— {BUSINESS.owner.name}, owner, Blouin Pest Services LLC</strong></p>

  <h2>Licensing</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>Licence</dt>
    <dd>Maine {BUSINESS.license.type}, number {BUSINESS.license.number}, in {BUSINESS.license.categories.join(' and ')}.</dd>
    <dt>Firm licence</dt>
    <dd>Held by Blouin Pest Services LLC. Ryan is the only applicator working under it.</dd>
    <dt>Insurance</dt>
    <dd>{BUSINESS.license.liability} liability coverage in force.</dd>
    <dt>Regulator</dt>
    <dd>Licensed and regulated by the {BUSINESS.license.authority}. <a href="/compliance/maine-pesticide-licensing/">What that means, and how to check any company</a>.</dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    Those two categories are the reason you will not find termite, wildlife or browntail moth work on this site. Maine licenses by
    category and an applicator may only treat in the categories they hold, so we tell you plainly when something is outside ours.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>One person, start to finish. The person who inspects your house is the person who treats it.</li>
    <li>Inspection before quotation, and the quote separates treatment from sealing and repair.</li>
    <li>Written record of every visit: found, applied, recommended.</li>
    <li>When the fix belongs to a carpenter, a roofer or a plumber, we say so instead of treating around it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we will not say</h2>
  <p>
    You will not find a "best in Maine" claim on this site. The review figure on the <a href="/reviews/">reviews page</a> is read
    from the Google Business Profile with the date it was taken, and {BUSINESS.customers} is Ryan's own figure rather than a
    rounded-up one. Where we offer a greener option it is named — {BUSINESS.greenOption} — rather than described with a vague
    environmental label that means whatever the reader wants it to mean.
  </p>

  <CallToAction />
</BaseLayout>
